meta {
  name: Presign Screenshot
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/bug-reports/screenshots/presign
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "filename": "leaderboard-stale.png",
    "contentType": "image/png",
    "size": 20480
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 201 || res.getStatus() === 200) {
    bru.setVar("bugScreenshotKey", res.getBody().key);
    bru.setVar("bugScreenshotUploadUrl", res.getBody().uploadUrl);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("returns a presigned PUT URL and a server-minted key", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("key");
    expect(body).to.have.property("uploadUrl");
    expect(body).to.have.property("expiresIn");
    expect(body.requiredHeaders["Content-Type"]).to.equal("image/png");
  });

  test("the key is namespaced to the caller, not just their agency", function () {
    // `agencies/<agencyId>/bug-reports/<userId>/…` — the user segment is what
    // stops one member of an agency attaching a colleague's upload.
    expect(res.getBody().key).to.match(/^agencies\/[0-9a-f]{24}\/bug-reports\/[0-9a-f]{24}\//);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /bug-reports/screenshots/presign — step 1 of 3

  Issues a short-lived **presigned PUT URL** so the browser uploads a screenshot
  straight to object storage. The bytes never pass through the API — there is no
  multer and no `FileInterceptor` anywhere in this codebase, and none should be
  added. Same chain as `Quote Recaps/Presign Quote Document` and
  `Platform Mailers/Presign Import`.

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`)
  - **Permission:** **none** — see below
  - **Data scope:** none (`@SkipTenant()`, `@SkipBranch()`)

  ## Why no permission at all

  This is the only authenticated write in the API that declares none. The people
  most likely to hit a bug are the ones whose page just 403'd, so gating the
  reporter on a module permission would silence exactly them. `@SkipTenant()` /
  `@SkipBranch()` are there so a **platform operator** — who has no agency and
  would otherwise be rejected by `TenantGuard` with "Agency context required" —
  can report a bug in the Super Admin panel.

  Reading the queue is what is gated: `platform:bugs:read`, in
  **Platform Bug Reports**.

  The abuse bound is the rate limit instead — `BUG_REPORT_RATE_LIMIT × 6` per
  minute on this route (six presigns per report, so a mis-picked file and a
  retry never lock someone out of submitting).

  ## Body
  | field       | type   | rules                                          |
  |-------------|--------|------------------------------------------------|
  | filename    | string | 1–255 chars                                    |
  | contentType | enum   | `image/png` \| `image/jpeg` \| `image/webp` \| `image/gif` |
  | size        | int    | > 0, ≤ 10 MB                                   |

  Narrower than the mailer CSV rule on purpose: every source of a screenshot (a
  file picker, a drag, a clipboard paste) reports a real `image/*` type, so
  widening it would only let non-images through.

  ## Response `201`
  ```json
  {
    "key": "agencies/<agencyId>/bug-reports/<userId>/2026/<uuid>-leaderboard-stale.png",
    "uploadUrl": "http://localhost:9000/sfa-uploads/agencies/...",
    "requiredHeaders": { "Content-Type": "image/png" },
    "expiresIn": 300
  }
  ```

  The key is **server-generated** and namespaced to the caller; `Create Bug
  Report` re-checks that prefix, so a key belonging to someone else is rejected.

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — bad content type, or over 10 MB.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired token.
  - `429 Too Many Requests` — over the per-minute limit.
  - `503 Service Unavailable` — object storage is not configured.
}
